 # Task list API specification
 
-Version: 1.1
+Version: 1.2
 
 Date: 2026-10-28
 
@@ -27,3 +27,12 @@ the identifiers deterministic while ensuring that no two tasks returned by the s
 `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`, and `remove` each accept either an ID or a title. When
 a string could name both an ID and a title, it is interpreted as an ID so a task is always reachable by
 its stable identifier.
+
+## Input validation
+
+Requirement: screens must not be able to add malformed tasks to a list.
+
+`add` and `rename` reject empty or whitespace-only titles and titles longer than 120 characters. `add`
+also rejects a priority other than `low`, `normal`, or `high`, and validates every supplied tag. `tag`
+rejects an empty tag or one containing a space. Invalid input returns an `invalid-input` error whose
+message explains the failing field; it does not change the list.
